     "systemPrompt": "Use MCP with action=list/add/edit/remove to manage configured MCP services; never ask users to paste secrets in chat, because add/edit opens a secure form for secret values. To add an HTTP (url) MCP server just pass name+url \u2014 the form shows one API-token field and auto-creates a standard 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' header; never pass, view, or hand-edit the token or any header, and only set authHeader for a non-standard header name (e.g. X-Api-Key). To use actual MCP server tools, call Finch ToolSearch with source:\"mcp\" first \u2014 mcp__<server>__<tool> names are never pre-loaded and will fail if called directly. ToolSearch connects matching servers, discovers their tools, and injects mcp__<server>__<tool> functions into the current run. Authorization can be granted per-tool (mcp__filesystem__read_file) or with a wildcard (mcp__filesystem__*).",
     "termsOfServiceUrl": "https://finchwork.app/terms",
     "toolMeta": {
      "name": "MCP"
     }
    },
